{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  GOD SQUAD — verse-index.liquid

  BANDS 2 and 3 of the Verse feature: the "Explore Verses" label and category
  chips, and the grid of verse cards beneath them.

  They are one section because the chips are DERIVED from the cards. The chip
  row is not a list the merchant types twice — it is the set of distinct
  categories the blocks actually carry, so a category with no card cannot
  appear and a card cannot be uncategorised into a chip that does not exist.
  Splitting them would put the derivation across a section boundary, where one
  section cannot read the other's blocks.

  THE CHIPS ARE HIDDEN UNTIL SCRIPT REVEALS THEM. Filtering is client side;
  with JavaScript off it cannot happen, and a row of controls that does nothing
  is worse than no row — it is a promise the page does not keep. So the markup
  ships them hidden and assets/verse-filter.js unhides them. Without script the
  page is every verse, which is the honest fallback.

  Sources of truth: the owner's approved Verse mockup, PHASE-2-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md,
  and sections/our-story.liquid for the house style.
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | strip

  assign surface_class = 'surface-light'
  if section.settings.surface == 'dark'
    assign surface_class = 'surface-dark'
  endif

  comment
    Collect the distinct categories the blocks carry, in block order.

    The handles list is delimited on BOTH sides of every entry — ',faith,' not
    'faith' — because Liquid's `contains` on a string is a substring test, and
    an undelimited 'faith' would match inside 'faithful' and silently drop the
    second category. The labels ride a parallel list so the chip shows what the
    merchant typed rather than the handle.
  endcomment
  assign cat_handles = ','
  assign cat_labels = ''
  assign cat_count = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    assign label = block.settings.category | strip
    if label != blank
      assign h = label | handle
      assign probe = ',' | append: h | append: ','
      unless cat_handles contains probe
        assign cat_handles = cat_handles | append: h | append: ','
        assign cat_labels = cat_labels | append: label | append: '|'
        assign cat_count = cat_count | plus: 1
      endunless
    endif
  endfor
  assign cat_label_list = cat_labels | split: '|'

  comment
    One category is not a filter. The chip row appears only when there is a
    choice to make, and only when the merchant has not turned it off.
  endcomment
  assign show_filter = false
  if section.settings.show_filter and cat_label_list.size > 1
    assign show_filter = true
  endif

  assign img_sizes = '(min-width: 1280px) 25vw, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw'

  assign classes = 'verse-index '
  assign classes = classes | append: surface_class
  assign classes = classes | append: ' verse-index--pt-' | append: section.settings.spacing_top
  assign classes = classes | append: ' verse-index--pb-' | append: section.settings.spacing_bottom
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  No cards and no heading means nothing to show. The editor always renders, so
  a merchant who has just added the section can see and configure it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if section.blocks.size == 0 and heading == blank and request.design_mode == false -%}
  {%- comment -%} Not configured yet: render nothing, and request nothing. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- else -%}

{{ 'section-verse-index.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- if show_filter -%}
  <script src="{{ 'verse-filter.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}

<div class="{{ classes }}" {% if section.settings.anchor_id != blank %}id="{{ section.settings.anchor_id | handle }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="verse-index__inner container">

    {%- comment -%} ---------------------------------------- BAND 2: the head {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="verse-index__head">
      {%- if heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="verse-index__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The long rule between the label and the chips. Decorative, so it is a
        span with aria-hidden rather than an <hr>, which would announce a
        thematic break that is not there.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="verse-index__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      {%- if show_filter -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Buttons, not links: they change what is on this page, they do not
          navigate, and there is no URL that represents the filtered state
          because nothing is re-fetched.

          aria-pressed, not aria-current: each chip is an independent toggle
          whose state is "this filter is on", and the APG's button pattern uses
          aria-pressed for exactly that. aria-current means "this is the one
          within a set that you are on", which is a navigation idea.

          The state is never colour alone (SC 1.4.1): the pressed chip also
          carries --weight-semibold against --weight-medium, the same way
          component-pagination.css:62-67 keeps the current page legible.

          role="group" with an accessible name, so the row announces as one
          thing rather than seven loose buttons.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div
          class="verse-index__filter"
          role="group"
          aria-label="{{ 'sections.verse_index.filter_label' | t }}"
          data-verse-filter
          hidden
        >
          <button type="button" class="verse-chip" data-verse-chip="all" aria-pressed="true">
            {{ 'sections.verse_index.all' | t }}
          </button>
          {%- for label in cat_label_list -%}
            {%- if label == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="verse-chip"
              data-verse-chip="{{ label | handle }}"
              aria-pressed="false"
            >
              {{ label | escape }}
            </button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} --------------------------------------- BAND 3: the cards {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ul class="verse-index__grid" role="list" data-verse-grid>
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign b_category = block.settings.category | strip
            assign b_quote = block.settings.quote | strip
            assign b_reference = block.settings.reference | strip
            assign b_label = block.settings.link_label | strip
            assign b_url = block.settings.link_url
            assign b_img = block.settings.image

            assign b_show_link = false
            if b_label != blank and b_url != blank
              assign b_show_link = true
            endif

            assign b_empty = false
            if b_quote == blank and b_img == blank and b_reference == blank
              assign b_empty = true
            endif
          -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            EVERY BLOCK RENDERS AN <li>, even an empty one, and the empty case is
            skipped only on the live storefront. A block that renders nothing
            renders no shopify_attributes either, so the Theme Editor has no
            element to outline, scroll to or fire shopify:block:select against —
            the merchant clicks Add verse, the canvas does not change, and the
            block is reachable only from the sidebar. That is a Phase 11 defect
            class, and this is the guard against it.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if b_empty and request.design_mode == false -%}
            {%- continue -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          <li
            class="verse-card{% if b_empty %} verse-card--empty{% endif %}"
            {% if b_category != blank %}data-verse-category="{{ b_category | handle }}"{% endif %}
            {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
          >
            <div class="verse-card__media">
              {%- if b_img != blank -%}
                {{
                  b_img
                  | image_url: width: 1200
                  | image_tag:
                    class: 'verse-card__image',
                    widths: '320, 480, 640, 900, 1200',
                    sizes: img_sizes,
                    loading: 'lazy',
                    decoding: 'async',
                    alt: b_img.alt
                }}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  The stand-ins cycle rather than repeat one file, so four cards
                  read as four photographs. Cycling on the block's own position
                  keeps a given card on a given file across reloads.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign fb_files = 'story.webp,tee.webp,hoodie.webp,cap.webp' | split: ','
                  assign fb_i = forloop.index0 | modulo: 4
                -%}
                {% render 'image-fallback',
                  file: fb_files[fb_i],
                  class: 'verse-card__image',
                  sizes: img_sizes,
                  width: 1200,
                  height: 1600
                %}
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- comment -%}
                THE SCRIM IS MANDATORY AND IS NOT A MERCHANT CHOICE — the same
                reasoning our-story.liquid:192-199 records. Cream copy sits over
                a photograph the theme has never seen, and a merchant who could
                switch it off would be switching off the only thing making the
                quote legible. Its alpha is derived, not chosen: see
                section-verse-index.css.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="verse-card__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            </div>

            <div class="verse-card__body">
              {%- if b_category != blank -%}
                <p class="verse-card__category">{{ b_category | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if b_quote != blank -%}
                <blockquote class="verse-card__quote">
                  <p>{{ b_quote | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
                </blockquote>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if b_reference != blank -%}
                <p class="verse-card__reference">{{ b_reference | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if b_show_link -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  The link's accessible name carries the reference as well as the
                  label, because four links all reading "Read verse" give a
                  screen-reader user a list of identical destinations (SC 2.4.4).
                  The visible label stays as the design has it.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <a
                  class="verse-card__link"
                  href="{{ b_url }}"
                  {% if b_reference != blank %}aria-label="{{ b_label | escape }}: {{ b_reference | escape }}"{% endif %}
                >
                  {{ b_label | escape }}
                  {% render 'icon-arrow', class: 'icon--sm' %}
                </a>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

      {%- if show_filter -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The filter's own live region. It is empty in the markup and stays
          empty until a chip is pressed, because a region created together with
          its content announces nothing — the same rule assets/cart.js records
          for announce(). It is section-local rather than the layout's
          #CartStatus, which belongs to the cart and must not be spoken over.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The attribute carries the SENTENCE, with a literal [count] the script
          substitutes. Same construction as locales "quantity": "Quantity:
          [count]" consumed by assets/cart.js — a sentence assembled in
          JavaScript cannot be translated, one carried in the locale file can.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p
          class="visually-hidden"
          role="status"
          data-verse-status="{{ 'sections.verse_index.count' | t | escape }}"
        ></p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if request.design_mode -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign notices = ''
        if section.blocks.size == 0
          assign notices = notices | append: 'no_blocks|'
        endif
        assign missing_img = 0
        assign missing_cat = 0
        assign missing_url = 0
        for block in section.blocks
          if block.settings.image == blank
            assign missing_img = missing_img | plus: 1
          endif
          if block.settings.category == blank
            assign missing_cat = missing_cat | plus: 1
          endif
          if block.settings.link_label != blank and block.settings.link_url == blank
            assign missing_url = missing_url | plus: 1
          endif
        endfor
        if missing_img > 0
          assign notices = notices | append: 'no_image|'
        endif
        if missing_cat > 0
          assign notices = notices | append: 'no_category|'
        endif
        if missing_url > 0
          assign notices = notices | append: 'no_link_url|'
        endif
        if section.settings.show_filter and cat_count == 1
          assign notices = notices | append: 'one_category|'
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if notices != blank -%}
        <div class="verse-index__notice">
          {%- if notices contains 'no_blocks' -%}
            <p>{{ 'sections.verse_index.no_blocks' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if notices contains 'no_image' -%}
            <p>{{ 'sections.verse_index.no_image' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if notices contains 'no_category' -%}
            <p>{{ 'sections.verse_index.no_category' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if notices contains 'no_link_url' -%}
            <p>{{ 'sections.verse_index.no_link_url' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if notices contains 'one_category' -%}
            <p>{{ 'sections.verse_index.one_category' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Explore Verses",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "verse-index-section",
  "max_blocks": 12,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Explore Verses"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_filter",
      "label": "Show category filter",
      "info": "The filter needs at least two different categories, and needs JavaScript. Without it every verse is shown.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "surface",
      "label": "Surface",
      "options": [
        { "value": "light", "label": "Cream" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Ink" }
      ],
      "default": "light"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spacing_top",
      "label": "Space above",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Tight" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "Standard" }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spacing_bottom",
      "label": "Space below",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Tight" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "Standard" }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor_id",
      "label": "Anchor",
      "info": "Lets a menu item link to this band."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "verse",
      "name": "Verse",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "category",
          "label": "Category",
          "info": "Becomes a filter chip. Verses sharing a category share a chip."
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "quote",
          "label": "Verse",
          "info": "Line breaks are kept."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "reference",
          "label": "Reference"
        },
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Image",
          "info": "Set alt text on the image itself in Content > Files."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "link_label",
          "label": "Link label"
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "link_url",
          "label": "Link",
          "info": "The link stays hidden until this is set."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Explore Verses",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Explore Verses",
        "show_filter": true,
        "surface": "light",
        "spacing_top": "standard",
        "spacing_bottom": "standard"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Faith",
            "quote": "“Walk by faith,\nnot by sight.”",
            "reference": "2 Corinthians 5:7",
            "link_label": "Read Verse"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Purpose",
            "quote": "“For I know the plans\nI have for you.”",
            "reference": "Jeremiah 29:11",
            "link_label": "Read Verse"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Courage",
            "quote": "“Be strong and\ncourageous.”",
            "reference": "Joshua 1:9",
            "link_label": "Read Verse"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Light",
            "quote": "“Let your light shine\nbefore others.”",
            "reference": "Matthew 5:16",
            "link_label": "Read Verse"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
